om/u/163303845?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal","html_url":"https://github.com/Uumutunal","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Uumutunal/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-10T18:39:37Z","updated_at":"2024-12-10T18:39:37Z","body":"On your model you have 2 UV sets, UVMap and UVMap.001, and in materials you're using UVMap.001, when you import it to godot it automatically uses the first UV set (UVMap). This is why you don't see the textures, if you remove the unused UV set from the model it works.\n\nRight one is imported without removing the unused UV set, left one i after I removed it.\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d34a99b5-a310-40d8-8a84-6fd6ecf7bd1b)\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2532589894/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120379682","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100172#issuecomment-3120379682","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100172","id":3120379682,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65_Tci","user":{"login":"TheSofox","id":3089525,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODk1MjU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3089525?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox","html_url":"https://github.com/TheSofox","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TheSofox/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T21:13:50Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T21:14:36Z","body":"Good catch. I had the exact same problem with another model (on v4.4.1.stable.official [49a5bc7b6] ) and when looking it up I found this bug report and confirmed I had two UVmaps. Deleting one fixed the problem.\n\nEven though the user has a clear workaround, this does seem like an bug. It makes intuitive sense that Godot would use whichever UV map was used to display the model, not just choose the first one in the list. Even Windows 3D Viewer uses the right UV map by default.\n\n<img width=\"1003\" height=\"841\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6595fb04-7951-49f3-8771-f16e13fac54d\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120379682/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120664127","html_url":"https://g